msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Exemplo de simulador em pequena escala {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Etapa 1: Mapear entradas clássicas para um problema quântico {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian and reference state {#hamiltonian-and-reference-state}"
msgstr "Hamiltoniano e estado de referência {#hamiltonian-and-reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses a 12-qubit open-boundary Heisenberg chain ($n=12$),\n"
msgstr "Este exemplo usa uma cadeia de Heisenberg de 12 qubits com fronteira aberta ($n=12$),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\left(X_iX_{i+1}+Y_iY_{i+1}+Z_iZ_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\left(X_iX_{i+1}+Y_iY_{i+1}+Z_iZ_{i+1}\\right),\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with a single-excitation product state\n"
msgstr "com um estado produto de excitação única\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=|000001000000\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=|000001000000\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"as the reference state.\n"
"Because the Heisenberg Hamiltonian defined above conserves the total number of excitations, the reference state stays in the single-excitation subspace, whose dimension grows only linearly with the number of qubits. We can therefore compute the exact ground-state energy efficiently, by diagonalizing the Hamiltonian restricted to that subspace, and use it purely as a diagnostic benchmark for the KQD estimate. The KQD workflow itself estimates projected matrix elements by using Qiskit primitives and solves the resulting projected problem classically.\n"
msgstr ""
"como estado de referência.\n"
"Como o Hamiltoniano de Heisenberg definido acima conserva o número total de excitações, o estado de referência permanece no subespaço de excitação única, cuja dimensão cresce apenas linearmente com o número de qubits. Podemos, portanto, calcular a energia exata do estado fundamental de forma eficiente, diagonalizando o Hamiltoniano restrito a esse subespaço, e usá-la puramente como um benchmark diagnóstico para a estimativa KQD. O próprio fluxo de trabalho KQD estima os elementos de matriz projetados usando primitivas do Qiskit e resolve o problema projetado resultante classicamente.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the parameters for the algorithm {#set-the-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"
msgstr "Definir os parâmetros do algoritmo {#set-the-parameters-for-the-algorithm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Based on the upper-bounds on the Hamiltonian norm, Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) heuristically suggests the time step $\\Delta t$ as $\\pi/\\|H\\|$.\n"
"Because the spectral norm $\\|H\\|$ is hard to compute, we instead use its upper bound:\n"
msgstr ""
"Com base nos limites superiores da norma do Hamiltoniano, a Ref. [\\[1\\]](#references) sugere heuristicamente o passo de tempo $\\Delta t$ como $\\pi/\\|H\\|$.\n"
"Como a norma espectral $\\|H\\|$ é difícil de calcular, usamos em vez disso o seu limite superior:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\|H\\| \\le \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\underbrace{\\|X_i X_{i+1}+Y_{i} Y_{i+1}+Z_{i} Z_{i+1}\\|}_{4 \\times 4 \\text{ matrix, easy to calculate the norm}} = 3(n-1).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\|H\\| \\le \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\\underbrace{\\|X_i X_{i+1}+Y_{i} Y_{i+1}+Z_{i} Z_{i+1}\\|}_{4 \\times 4 \\text{ matrix, easy to calculate the norm}} = 3(n-1).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We set the Krylov dimension to $r=10$ and the number of Trotter steps per time step to $5$: a large enough Krylov space to resolve the low-lying spectrum while keeping the deepest circuit ($t_{\\max}=(r-1)\\Delta t$) affordable, and enough Trotter steps to keep the discretization error small at that deepest circuit.\n"
msgstr "Definimos a dimensão de Krylov como $r=10$ e o número de passos de Trotter por passo de tempo como $5$: um espaço de Krylov grande o suficiente para resolver o espectro de baixa energia, mantendo o circuito mais profundo ($t_{\\max}=(r-1)\\Delta t$) viável, e passos de Trotter suficientes para manter o erro de discretização pequeno nesse circuito mais profundo.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build circuit {#build-circuit}"
msgstr "Construir circuito {#build-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we build the circuits to estimate the matrix elements $\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}$ and $\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}$.\n"
"Because all powers of $H$ commute, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui, construímos os circuitos para estimar os elementos de matriz $\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}$ e $\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}$.\n"
"Como todas as potências de $H$ comutam, temos\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|H e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{H}_{0,\\ell-k},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|H e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{H}_{0,\\ell-k},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{S}_{0,\\ell-k}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Such matrices where the elements depend on the index differences in this manner are called *Toeplitz* and can be reconstructed from first-row elements indexed by $d=\\ell-k$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_{0}|e^{-i(\\ell-k)\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\mathcal{S}_{0,\\ell-k}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"Such matrices where the elements depend on the index differences in this manner are called *Toeplitz* and can be reconstructed from first-row elements indexed by $d=\\ell-k$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we present the circuit, called **extended-swap-test**, which prepares\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $|\\psi_d\\rangle=e^{-id\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui, apresentamos o circuito, chamado **teste de troca estendido**, que prepara\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"onde $|\\psi_d\\rangle=e^{-id\\Delta tH}|\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference state {#reference-state}"
msgstr "Estado de referência {#reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We prepare the reference state $|\\psi_0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Preparamos o estado de referência $|\\psi_0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/fb2879c5-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/fb2879c5-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time evolution {#time-evolution}"
msgstr "Evolução temporal {#time-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Realize the time-evolution operator generated by the Hamiltonian, approximated by simple [Lie-Trotterization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter).\n"
msgstr "Realize o operador de evolução temporal gerado pelo Hamiltoniano, aproximado por [Lie-Trotterização](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) simples.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/017b8548-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/017b8548-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extended swap test circuit [\\[3\\]](#references) {#extended-swap-test-circuit-3references}"
msgstr "Circuito de teste de troca estendido [\\[3\\]](#references) {#extended-swap-test-circuit-3references}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit first prepares the reference state on the system register while the ancilla remains in $|0\\rangle$:\n"
msgstr "O circuito primeiro prepara o estado de referência no registro do sistema enquanto o ancilla permanece em $|0\\rangle$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_{0}\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_{0}\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then, applying a Hadamard gate to the ancilla creates a coherent superposition of two branches:\n"
msgstr "Em seguida, aplicar uma porta Hadamard ao ancilla cria uma superposição coerente de dois ramos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, the controlled time-evolution gate applies:\n"
msgstr "Finalmente, a porta de evolução temporal controlada se aplica:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t=d\\Delta t) = e^{-id\\Delta t H}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t=d\\Delta t) = e^{-id\\Delta t H}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "only when the ancilla is in the $|1\\rangle$ branch. Therefore,\n"
msgstr "apenas quando o ancilla está no ramo $|1\\rangle$. Portanto,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next code block, we implement:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Psi(t)\\rangle = \\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"which will be assigned as $t=d\\Delta t$ for $d=1,\\cdots r-1$ in the execution step.\n"
msgstr ""
"No próximo bloco de código, implementamos:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Psi(t)\\rangle = \\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"que será atribuído como $t=d\\Delta t$ para $d=1,\\cdots r-1$ na etapa de execução.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/1260f66a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/1260f66a-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observables {#observables}"
msgstr "Observáveis {#observables}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For any Hermitian system observable $O$, here we set the observables to calculate:\n"
msgstr "Para qualquer observável hermitiano do sistema $O$, aqui definimos os observáveis a calcular:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"z=\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"z=\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is because $O=I$ gives the overlap element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle$, while $O=H$ gives the Hamiltonian element $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Isso ocorre porque $O=I$ fornece o elemento de sobreposição $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle$, enquanto $O=H$ fornece o elemento Hamiltoniano $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}=\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using $X=|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$, we have\n"
msgstr "Usando $X=|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$, temos\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|X\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(X\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{z+z^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|X\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(X\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{z+z^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Re} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Re} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, using $Y=-i|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$,\n"
msgstr "Da mesma forma, usando $Y=-i|0\\rangle\\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle\\langle 0|$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(Y\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"-i\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"i\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{-iz+iz^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\langle \\Psi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O| \\Psi_{0d} \\rangle\n"
"&=\n"
"\\left(\\frac{\\langle0|\\langle\\psi_0| + \\langle1| \\langle\\psi_d|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)(Y\\otimes O)\\left(\\frac{|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_d\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"-i\\langle \\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"i\\langle \\psi_d|O|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\frac{-iz+iz^*}{2}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Im} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Im} z.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|X\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Portanto, temos\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|X\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\langle \\Phi_{0d}|Y\\otimes O|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\operatorname{Im}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\operatorname{Im}\\langle\\psi_0|O|\\psi_d\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, for each state $|\\Psi_{0d}\\rangle$, we need to measure:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"X \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"X \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{H}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{H}_{0d}.\\\\\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Finalmente, para cada estado $|\\Psi_{0d}\\rangle$, precisamos medir:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"X \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes I \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{S}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"X \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Re}\\mathcal{H}_{0d},\\\\\n"
"Y \\otimes H \\text{ for } \\operatorname{Im}\\mathcal{H}_{0d}.\\\\\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the estimation of the $\\mathcal{H}$ matrix elements, the number of Pauli terms is much larger than that for the $\\mathcal{S}$ matrix elements.\n"
msgstr "Para a estimativa dos elementos de matriz $\\mathcal{H}$, o número de termos de Pauli é muito maior do que para os elementos de matriz $\\mathcal{S}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now reduce the number of measured Hamiltonian terms by using a shifting technique [\\[4\\]](#references).\n"
"We split the Hamiltonian as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Agora podemos reduzir o número de termos Hamiltonianos medidos usando uma técnica de deslocamento [\\[4\\]](#references).\n"
"Dividimos o Hamiltoniano como:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H = (H-T) + T,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H = (H-T) + T,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $T$ is chosen such that the reference state is its eigenstate,\n"
msgstr "onde $T$ é escolhido de forma que o estado de referência seja seu autoestado,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then,\n"
msgstr "Then,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{0d}\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|T|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{0d}\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|H|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|T|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\langle\\psi_0|\\psi_d\\rangle \\\\\n"
"&=\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}.\n"
"\\end{align*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here,\n"
msgstr "Here,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\psi_0|(H-T)|\\psi_d\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is the shifted Hamiltonian matrix element.\n"
"Therefore, we only need to measure $X\\otimes (H-T)$ and $Y\\otimes (H-T)$.\n"
"The contribution from $T$ is reconstructed classically using the already measured overlap matrix element $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"é o elemento de matriz Hamiltoniano deslocado.\n"
"Portanto, só precisamos medir $X\\otimes (H-T)$ e $Y\\otimes (H-T)$.\n"
"A contribuição de $T$ é reconstruída classicamente usando o elemento de matriz de sobreposição $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$ já medido.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this example, a natural choice is the diagonal part of the Heisenberg Hamiltonian,\n"
msgstr "Neste exemplo, uma escolha natural é a parte diagonal do Hamiltoniano de Heisenberg,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the reference state is a computational-basis state, it is an eigenstate of every $Z_iZ_{i+1}$ term.\n"
msgstr "Como o estado de referência é um estado da base computacional, ele é um autoestado de cada termo $Z_iZ_{i+1}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, a more advantageous choice is to include not only the diagonal $ZZ$ terms, but also the $XX+YY$ terms that annihilate the reference state.\n"
msgstr "No entanto, uma escolha mais vantajosa é incluir não apenas os termos diagonais $ZZ$, mas também os termos $XX+YY$ que anulam o estado de referência.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each neighboring pair, the operator $XX+YY$ satisfies\n"
msgstr "Para cada par vizinho, o operador $XX+YY$ satisfaz\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|00\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|11\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|00\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|11\\rangle = 0,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "and\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|01\\rangle = 2|10\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|10\\rangle = 2|01\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"(XX+YY)|01\\rangle = 2|10\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"(XX+YY)|10\\rangle = 2|01\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, the $XX+YY$ term contributes only when the two neighboring qubits have different occupations in the reference bitstring.\n"
"If the two qubits are both $0$ or both $1$, the term annihilates the reference state and can also be shifted out.\n"
msgstr ""
"Portanto, o termo $XX+YY$ contribui apenas quando os dois qubits vizinhos têm ocupações diferentes na cadeia de bits de referência.\n"
"Se os dois qubits forem ambos $0$ ou ambos $1$, o termo anula o estado de referência e também pode ser deslocado.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $|\\psi_{\\rm ref}\\rangle = |z_0\\cdots z_{n-1}\\rangle$, where $z_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Thus, we can choose\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{z_i={z_{i+1}}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Seja $|\\psi_{\\rm ref}\\rangle = |z_0\\cdots z_{n-1}\\rangle$, onde $z_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Assim, podemos escolher\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-2} Z_iZ_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"\\sum_{z_i={z_{i+1}}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This operator still satisfies\n"
msgstr "Este operador ainda satisfaz\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"T|\\psi_0\\rangle = \\tau |\\psi_0\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"because the $ZZ$ terms act diagonally on $|\\psi_0\\rangle$, while the shifted $XX+YY$ terms give zero.\n"
"The corresponding eigenvalue is therefore determined only by the $ZZ$ terms,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\tau = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\n"
"(-1)^{z_i}\n"
"(-1)^{z_{i+1}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"porque os termos $ZZ$ atuam diagonalmente em $|\\psi_0\\rangle$, enquanto os termos deslocados $XX+YY$ dão zero.\n"
"O autovalor correspondente é, portanto, determinado apenas pelos termos $ZZ$,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\tau = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-2}\n"
"(-1)^{z_i}\n"
"(-1)^{z_{i+1}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this choice, the shifted Hamiltonian becomes:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H-T = \\sum_{z_i\\ne z_{i+1}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Com essa escolha, o Hamiltoniano deslocado se torna:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"H-T = \\sum_{z_i\\ne z_{i+1}}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"X_iX_{i+1}\n"
"+\n"
"Y_iY_{i+1}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a result, only the edges with different occupations in the reference state need to be measured.\n"
"All $ZZ$ terms and all inactive $XX+YY$ terms are reconstructed through the overlap contribution $\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}$, or give zero contribution by construction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Como resultado, apenas as arestas com ocupações diferentes no estado de referência precisam ser medidas.\n"
"Todos os termos $ZZ$ e todos os termos inativos $XX+YY$ são reconstruídos por meio da contribuição de sobreposição $\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}$, ou dão contribuição zero por construção.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This gives a smaller observable than shifting only the diagonal part.\n"
"In particular, for a computational-basis reference state with a localized excitation, only the edges adjacent to the excitation remain in $H-T$.\n"
"Therefore, the number of Pauli terms in $X\\otimes(H-T)$ and $Y\\otimes(H-T)$ can be substantially reduced, while the reconstructed matrix element\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Isso fornece um observável menor do que deslocar apenas a parte diagonal.\n"
"Em particular, para um estado de referência da base computacional com uma excitação localizada, apenas as arestas adjacentes à excitação permanecem em $H-T$.\n"
"Portanto, o número de termos de Pauli em $X\\otimes(H-T)$ e $Y\\otimes(H-T)$ pode ser substancialmente reduzido, enquanto o elemento de matriz reconstruído\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\widetilde{\\mathcal{H}}_{0d}\n"
"+\n"
"\\tau \\mathcal{S}_{0d}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "remains exactly the same.\n"
msgstr "permanece exatamente o mesmo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Etapa 2: Otimizar o problema para execução em hardware quântico {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we turn the abstract extended-swap-test circuit into a hardware-oriented template.\n"
"Before that, we further optimize the circuit in the abstract level first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Agora transformamos o circuito abstrato de teste de troca estendido em um modelo orientado a hardware.\n"
"Antes disso, otimizamos ainda mais o circuito primeiro em nível abstrato.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare Hamiltonian term ordering {#compare-hamiltonian-term-ordering}"
msgstr "Comparar a ordenação de termos Hamiltonianos {#compare-hamiltonian-term-ordering}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we compare different orderings of the Pauli terms in the Heisenberg Hamiltonian for the Hamiltonian simulation.\n"
"The Hamiltonian itself is unchanged, but the ordering affects how the product-formula circuit is generated and how much the structure can be parallelized in the circuit.\n"
"For example, the naive ordering lists all nearest-neighbor $XX$ terms, then all $YY$ terms, then all $ZZ$ terms.\n"
"This places adjacent edges such as $(0,1)$ and $(1,2)$ next to each other, so they cannot be executed in parallel.\n"
"The even-then-odd ordering visits disjoint even edges first, followed by odd edges, which exposes parallel two-qubit layers.\n"
"The even-odd edge-grouped ordering goes one step further: for each edge, it keeps the local $XX$, $YY$, and $ZZ$ terms together, while still visiting even edges before odd edges.\n"
"We expect the even-then-odd and even-odd edge-grouped orderings to reduce circuit depth by exposing parallel two-qubit layers, and the edge-grouped ordering to additionally reduce the Trotter error because the local two-qubit interaction on the same edge is handled as a compact block.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primeiro, comparamos diferentes ordenações dos termos de Pauli no Hamiltoniano de Heisenberg para a simulação Hamiltoniana.\n"
"O próprio Hamiltoniano permanece inalterado, mas a ordenação afeta como o circuito de fórmula de produto é gerado e o quanto a estrutura pode ser paralelizada no circuito.\n"
"Por exemplo, a ordenação ingênua lista todos os termos $XX$ de vizinhos mais próximos, depois todos os termos $YY$, depois todos os termos $ZZ$.\n"
"Isso coloca arestas adjacentes, como $(0,1)$ e $(1,2)$, uma ao lado da outra, de modo que não podem ser executadas em paralelo.\n"
"A ordenação par-depois-ímpar visita primeiro arestas pares disjuntas, seguidas pelas arestas ímpares, o que expõe camadas de dois qubits paralelas.\n"
"A ordenação agrupada por aresta par-ímpar vai um passo além: para cada aresta, mantém os termos locais $XX$, $YY$ e $ZZ$ juntos, ainda visitando arestas pares antes das ímpares.\n"
"Esperamos que as ordenações par-depois-ímpar e agrupada por aresta par-ímpar reduzam a profundidade do circuito ao expor camadas de dois qubits paralelas, e que a ordenação agrupada por aresta reduza adicionalmente o erro de Trotter porque a interação local de dois qubits na mesma aresta é tratada como um bloco compacto.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Pauli evolutions with different term ordering](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/ham_ordering.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Pauli evolutions with different term ordering](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/ham_ordering.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Hamiltonian ordering also affects the Trotter error.\n"
"If we place noncommuting terms next to each other, the basis transitions occur more often, which induces more Trotter error.\n"
"By grouping terms that require the same Pauli-basis transformation, redundant basis-changes can be avoided.\n"
msgstr ""
"A ordenação do Hamiltoniano também afeta o erro de Trotter.\n"
"Se colocarmos termos que não comutam um ao lado do outro, as transições de base ocorrem com mais frequência, o que induz mais erro de Trotter.\n"
"Ao agrupar termos que exigem a mesma transformação de base de Pauli, mudanças de base redundantes podem ser evitadas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the comparison uses the largest evolution time that appears in the first-row Krylov estimates,\n"
"$t_{\\max} = (r-1)\\Delta t,$\n"
"using the same transpilation condition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui, a comparação usa o maior tempo de evolução que aparece nas estimativas de Krylov da primeira linha,\n"
"$t_{\\max} = (r-1)\\Delta t,$\n"
"usando a mesma condição de transpilação.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to measure the Trotter error, we use **process infidelity** between the Trotterized circuit and the exact Hamiltonian evolution,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\text{Infidelity}(U,V)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Para medir o erro de Trotter, usamos a **infidelidade do processo** entre o circuito trotterizado e a evolução Hamiltoniana exata,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\text{Infidelity}(U,V)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1-F(U,V)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"1-F(U,V)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1 - \\frac{|\\operatorname{Tr}(U^\\dagger V)|^2}{d^2},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d=2^n$ is the dimension of the Hilbert space.\n"
msgstr ""
"1 - \\frac{|\\operatorname{Tr}(U^\\dagger V)|^2}{d^2},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d=2^n$ is the dimension of the Hilbert space.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This diagnostic uses dense matrices, so it is suitable for this small 12-qubit example but not intended as a scalable subroutine.\n"
msgstr "Este diagnóstico usa matrizes densas, portanto é adequado para este pequeno exemplo de 12 qubits, mas não se destina a ser uma subrotina escalável.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We first keep the synthesis rule fixed to one first-order Trotter step and vary only the Pauli-term ordering.\n"
"The goal of this comparison is mainly to see how much circuit depth and two-qubit cost can be reduced by exposing disjoint nearest-neighbor edges to the transpiler.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primeiro mantemos a regra de síntese fixa em um passo de Trotter de primeira ordem e variamos apenas a ordenação dos termos de Pauli.\n"
"O objetivo desta comparação é principalmente ver o quanto a profundidade do circuito e o custo de dois qubits podem ser reduzidos ao expor arestas disjuntas de vizinhos mais próximos ao transpilador.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-1.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-3.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/21eaab38-5.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At `reps=1`, we observe that even-then-odd and even-odd edge-grouped orderings both collapse the depth from 15 to 6 by exposing parallel two-qubit layers, while the two-qubit gate count stays the same across all three orderings.\n"
"However, all three orderings have infidelity close to 1, so we sweep the number of Trotter repetitions to separate the orderings more clearly.\n"
"As the number of repetitions grows, the infidelity of `even-odd edge-grouped` ordering drops faster than the other two, reaching 0.045 at `reps=8` versus 0.075 for naive and even-then-odd ordering.\n"
msgstr ""
"Em `reps=1`, observamos que tanto a ordenação par-depois-ímpar quanto a agrupada por aresta par-ímpar reduzem a profundidade de 15 para 6 ao expor camadas de dois qubits paralelas, enquanto a contagem de portas de dois qubits permanece a mesma nas três ordenações.\n"
"No entanto, as três ordenações têm infidelidade próxima de 1, então variamos o número de repetições de Trotter para separar as ordenações de forma mais clara.\n"
"À medida que o número de repetições aumenta, a infidelidade da ordenação `even-odd edge-grouped` cai mais rápido do que as outras duas, atingindo 0,045 em `reps=8` contra 0,075 para a ordenação ingênua e a par-depois-ímpar.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare product-formula synthesis {#compare-product-formula-synthesis}"
msgstr "Comparar a síntese de fórmula de produto {#compare-product-formula-synthesis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we explore different advanced settings of Trotterization, with the fixed Hamiltonian ordering to the even-odd edge-grouped ordering.\n"
"We consider first-order Lie-Trotter, second-order Suzuki-Trotter, and fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, exploramos diferentes configurações avançadas de trotterização, com a ordenação Hamiltoniana fixa na ordenação agrupada por aresta par-ímpar.\n"
"Consideramos Lie-Trotter de primeira ordem, Suzuki-Trotter de segunda ordem e Suzuki-Trotter de quarta ordem.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lie-Trotter gives the shallowest circuit but has the largest error, while the fourth-order Suzuki-Trotter is more accurate but increases the circuit depth.\n"
"For the rest of the tutorial, we choose second-order Suzuki-Trotter because it gives a small-depth circuit while substantially reducing the Trotter error relative to the first-order formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"O Lie-Trotter fornece o circuito mais raso, mas tem o maior erro, enquanto o Suzuki-Trotter de quarta ordem é mais preciso, mas aumenta a profundidade do circuito.\n"
"Para o restante do tutorial, escolhemos o Suzuki-Trotter de segunda ordem porque ele fornece um circuito de pequena profundidade enquanto reduz substancialmente o erro de Trotter em relação à fórmula de primeira ordem.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove the controlled time-evolution gate {#remove-the-controlled-time-evolution-gate}"
msgstr "Remover a porta de evolução temporal controlada {#remove-the-controlled-time-evolution-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the extended swap test, controlling time evolution with a single ancilla qubit requires the ancilla to control many gates across the system.\n"
"This can introduce substantial routing overhead and, in the worst case, effectively requires all-to-one connectivity.\n"
"To avoid this, further optimization is possible by replacing the controlled time-evolution gate with a control-free version, exploiting the symmetry of the Hamiltonian.\n"
"Let's observe the following circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"No teste de troca estendido, controlar a evolução temporal com um único qubit ancilla exige que o ancilla controle muitas portas em todo o sistema.\n"
"Isso pode introduzir uma sobrecarga substancial de roteamento e, no pior caso, exige efetivamente conectividade de todos para um.\n"
"Para evitar isso, é possível uma otimização adicional substituindo a porta de evolução temporal controlada por uma versão livre de controle, explorando a simetria do Hamiltoniano.\n"
"Vamos observar o seguinte circuito.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![circuit optimization](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/circuit_opt.avif)\n"
msgstr "![circuit optimization](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/circuit_opt.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $B_{\\rm ref}$ prepares the reference state, $B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle = |\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Aqui, $B_{\\rm ref}$ prepara o estado de referência, $B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle = |\\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of first preparing $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)|\\psi_0\\rangle$ and then applying $U(t)$ only on the $|1\\rangle$ branch, the circuit directly prepares the two branches as\n"
msgstr "Em vez de primeiro preparar $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)|\\psi_0\\rangle$ e depois aplicar $U(t)$ apenas no ramo $|1\\rangle$, o circuito prepara diretamente os dois ramos como\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle|\\psi_d\\rangle ,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where\n"
msgstr "where\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = U(d\\Delta t)|\\psi_0\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit first applies a Hadamard gate to the ancilla and prepares the reference state only on the $|1\\rangle$ branch:\n"
msgstr "O circuito primeiro aplica uma porta Hadamard ao ancilla e prepara o estado de referência apenas no ramo $|1\\rangle$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle B_{\\rm ref}|0^n\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then the uncontrolled time-evolution operator is applied to both branches:\n"
msgstr "Em seguida, o operador de evolução temporal não controlado é aplicado a ambos os ramos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the Hamiltonian preserves the excitation number, we can see that $|0^n\\rangle$ is its eigenstate, and thus\n"
"the evolution operator only accumulates a phase under the Hamiltonian:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t)|0^n\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Como o Hamiltoniano preserva o número de excitações, podemos ver que $|0^n\\rangle$ é seu autoestado, e portanto\n"
"o operador de evolução acumula apenas uma fase sob o Hamiltoniano:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"U(t)|0^n\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0^n\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0^n\\rangle .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore,\n"
msgstr "Therefore,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{|0\\rangle U(t)|0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |0^n\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, $B_{\\rm ref}$ is applied only on the $|0\\rangle$ branch.\n"
msgstr "Em seguida, $B_{\\rm ref}$ é aplicado apenas no ramo $|0\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this point, the two branches have an extra relative phase. To remove it, we apply the ancilla phase gate\n"
msgstr "Neste ponto, os dois ramos têm uma fase relativa extra. Para removê-la, aplicamos a porta de fase do ancilla\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"P(-E_{\\rm vac}t)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"P(-E_{\\rm vac}t)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This transforms the state as\n"
msgstr "Isso transforma o estado como\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle + |1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\longrightarrow\n"
"\\frac{e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|0\\rangle |\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"e^{-iE_{\\rm vac}t}|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, up to an irrelevant global phase, we finally prepared\n"
msgstr "Assim, a menos de uma fase global irrelevante, finalmente preparamos\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"|\\Phi_{0d}\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\n"
"|0\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"+\n"
"|1\\rangle U(t)|\\psi_0\\rangle\n"
"}{\\sqrt{2}} .\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the next code block, we implement this control-free circuit.\n"
msgstr "No próximo bloco de código, implementamos este circuito livre de controle.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/790e5e0c-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/krylov-quantum-diagonalization/extracted-outputs/790e5e0c-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation {#transpilation}"
msgstr "Transpilação {#transpilation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, we transpile the controlled- and control-free circuits to become executable on the hardware.\n"
"Let's compare the result of the transpiled circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Agora, transpilamos os circuitos controlado e livre de controle para que se tornem executáveis no hardware.\n"
"Vamos comparar o resultado dos circuitos transpilados.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Etapa 3: Executar usando primitivos do Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next step is to submit the same parameterized circuit for several values of $d$. For each $d$, we estimate four expectation values: $X\\otimes I$, $Y\\otimes I$, $X\\otimes (H-T)$, and $Y\\otimes (H-T)$. These four numbers are then combined into the complex first-row elements $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$ and $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}$.\n"
msgstr "O próximo passo é submeter o mesmo circuito parametrizado para vários valores de $d$. Para cada $d$, estimamos quatro valores esperados: $X\\otimes I$, $Y\\otimes I$, $X\\otimes (H-T)$, e $Y\\otimes (H-T)$. Esses quatro números são então combinados nos elementos complexos da primeira linha $\\mathcal{S}_{0d}$ e $\\mathcal{H}_{0d}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $\\mathcal{S}_{00}=1$ and $\\mathcal{H}_{00}=\\langle\\psi_{0}|(H-T)|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\langle\\psi_{0}|H|\\psi_{0}\\rangle-\\tau$ can be classically calculated since $\\lvert\\psi_0\\rangle$ is sparse, so we skip the $d=0$ case.\n"
msgstr "Aqui, $\\mathcal{S}_{00}=1$ e $\\mathcal{H}_{00}=\\langle\\psi_{0}|(H-T)|\\psi_{0}\\rangle=\\langle\\psi_{0}|H|\\psi_{0}\\rangle-\\tau$ podem ser calculados classicamente, já que $\\lvert\\psi_0\\rangle$ é esparso, então pulamos o caso $d=0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Passo 4: Pós-processar e retornar o resultado no formato clássico desejado {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After estimating the projected matrices, we regularize and solve the GEVP\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c} = E\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"The smallest generalized eigenvalue gives the KQD estimate of the ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"Depois de estimar as matrizes projetadas, regularizamos e resolvemos o GEVP\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c} = E\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"O menor autovalor generalizado fornece a estimativa KQD da energia do estado fundamental.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we solve the generalized eigenvalue problem using the matrices reconstructed from the circuit estimates.\n"
"In an ideal statevector calculation with exact real-time evolution, this should reproduce the exact projected result.\n"
"In practice, deviations can come from Trotterization, sampling error, and numerical instability of the overlap matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Agora resolvemos o problema de autovalor generalizado usando as matrizes reconstruídas a partir das estimativas do circuito.\n"
"Em um cálculo ideal de vetor de estado com evolução exata em tempo real, isso deve reproduzir o resultado projetado exato.\n"
"Na prática, os desvios podem vir da trotterização, do erro de amostragem e da instabilidade numérica da matriz de sobreposição.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We observe how the energy converges as we increase the dimension of the Krylov subspace.\n"
msgstr "Observamos como a energia converge à medida que aumentamos a dimensão do subespaço de Krylov.\n"

